Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Aurora: the HD look's in-between frames see through the
 in-between camera

The HD look's shadows and lights (sun and cloud shadows, edge light, torch
light) are worked out from the game's camera, which the game thread sets at
each retrace and the render thread read when it drew the effects. With
Smooth Motion an in-between frame's scenery is where the camera was part of
the way from the frame before, but its effects were drawn from the latest
camera, so as the camera turned the shadows slid against the scenery.

The real frame's effects now keep the camera they were drawn from with the
frame, and each in-between frame draws from that camera moved as its
matrices move the scenery: frame_interp's camera motion D and its part P at
the step give the inverse view V^-1 * D * P^-1. The time for the cloud
shadows' drift goes between the two frames' as well. Without a camera motion
for the frame (its scenery blended from each draw's own matrices) an
in-between frame keeps the real frame's camera, as before.
